            "review_title": "Review at Dotori Dining",
            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n0\nCome hungry and/or kuchisabishii (lonely mouth)\nMar 2026 • Family\nLocated in the hip internal lane (or \"Hẻm\") of Thao Dien 28 (huge compound inside),\nDotori Dining is one of the first shops you'll see when you walk into this slice of haven.\n\nIf you feel hungry and/or kuchisabishii (we loved that they put this uniquely Japanese word on their window as part of their outdoor decor), you would wanna come here. Because the food here is absolutely satisfying (though not the healthiest!).\n\nAlso loved that their menu is in-your-face - just 15 main dishes and they all look good. Ordered: Nikomi Burger comes in a stew in a cast iron pot over fire, Maze pasta looked really unassuming but simply umami-MAX, 80s Retro Tonkatsu is crazy large, Eggs Benedict Pasta is as one can imagine, slurpishly good. Various Donburis with their respective mountains of tempura looked freakishly good but sinful.\n\nOnly bad thing - perpetually crowded, with the loud music, all the noise probably might give you a headache.\nRead more\nWritten June 23, 2026",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
